-          "quote": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$, where $\\mathbb F=\\mathbb R$ or $\\mathbb C$. Put $p=\\min(m,n)$ and $M=\\max(m,n)$. If $m\\ge n$, set $C=A$; if $m<n$, set $C=A^*$. Thus $C\\in\\mathbb F^{M\\times p}$.\n\nThe algorithm initializes $C_0=C$, $U=I_M$, and $V=I_p$. For $k=1,\\ldots,p$, in this order:\n\n1. Let $x=C_{k:M,k}$. If $x=0$, use the identity left transformation. Otherwise choose $\\phi=x_1/|x_1|$ when $x_1\\ne0$ and $\\phi=1$ when $x_1=0$, set $\\alpha=-\\phi\\|x\\|_2$, $v=x-\\alpha e_1$, and $h=v/\\|v\\|_2$. Use the Householder reflector $H=I-2hh^*$ on rows $k:M$. Update $C\\leftarrow H^*C$ on those rows and update $U\\leftarrow U\\operatorname{diag}(I_{k-1},H)$.\n2. If $k<p$, let $y=C_{k,k+1:p}^*$. If $y=0$, use the identity right transformation. Otherwise apply the same phase and normalization rule to $y$ to form the Householder reflector $G$, then apply $C\\leftarrow C\\operatorname{diag}(I_k,G)$ and $V\\leftarrow V\\operatorname{diag}(I_k,G)$.\n\nThe exact arithmetic output is the leading $p\\times p$ upper bidiagonal block $B$ of $C$, together with $U,V$. For $m\\ge n$ the output relation is $U^*AV=\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$. For $m<n$ it is $U^*A^*V=\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$; equivalently $A=V\\begin{bmatrix}B^*&0\\end{bmatrix}U^*$.\n\nIn finite precision, each left/right reflector uses [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]], including its real/complex scaled formation, range checks and exact target-column/row zero writes. This is the arithmetic realization of the exact steps above. A zero active vector takes the identity branch. Any nonfinite intermediate or overflow returns `range-failure` with the partial factors; otherwise return `success`, $B,U,V$, the reconstruction residual $\\|C-U\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}V^*\\|_F$, and the two orthogonality residuals $\\|U^*U-I\\|_F$ and $\\|V^*V-I\\|_F$. These reported residuals are computed quantities, not certified bounds by themselves. Matrix residuals use the Frobenius norm defined in [[def-frobenius-matrix-norm]].",
+          "quote": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$, where $\\mathbb F=\\mathbb R$ or $\\mathbb C$. Put $p=\\min(m,n)$ and $M=\\max(m,n)$. If $m\\ge n$, set $C=A$; if $m<n$, set $C=A^*$. Thus $C\\in\\mathbb F^{M\\times p}$.\n\nSave the input as $C_0=C$ and initialize $U=I_M$, $V=I_p$, and empty ordered lists of stored local left and right transformations. For $k=1,\\ldots,p$, in this order:\n\n1. Let $x=C_{k:M,k}$. If $x=0$, use the identity left transformation. Otherwise choose $\\phi=x_1/|x_1|$ when $x_1\\ne0$ and $\\phi=1$ when $x_1=0$, set $\\alpha=-\\phi\\|x\\|_2$, $v=x-\\alpha e_1$, and $h=v/\\|v\\|_2$. Use the Householder reflector $H=I-2hh^*$ on rows $k:M$. Update $C\\leftarrow H^*C$ on those rows and append this local transformation to the left list. In exact arithmetic update $U\\leftarrow U\\operatorname{diag}(I_{k-1},H)$. In finite precision update columns $k:M$ of the dense accumulator $U$ by right application of the same stored local reflector data, using the separate-block branch of [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]] and making no target-zero write to $U$.\n2. If $k<p$, let $y=C_{k,k+1:p}^*$. If $y=0$, use the identity right transformation. Otherwise apply the same phase and normalization rule to $y$ to form the Householder reflector $G$, then apply $C\\leftarrow C\\operatorname{diag}(I_k,G)$ and append this local transformation to the right list. In exact arithmetic update $V\\leftarrow V\\operatorname{diag}(I_k,G)$. In finite precision update columns $k+1:p$ of the dense accumulator $V$ by right application of the same stored local reflector data, using the separate-block branch of [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]] and making no target-zero write to $V$.\n\nThe exact arithmetic output is the leading $p\\times p$ upper bidiagonal block $B$ of $C$, together with $U,V$. For $m\\ge n$ the output relation is $U^*AV=\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$. For $m<n$ it is $U^*A^*V=\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$; equivalently $A=V\\begin{bmatrix}B^*&0\\end{bmatrix}U^*$.\n\nIn finite precision, each left/right reflector uses [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]], including its real/complex scaled formation, range checks and exact target-column/row zero writes. This is the arithmetic realization of the exact steps above. A zero active vector takes the identity branch. Any nonfinite intermediate or overflow returns `range-failure` with the partial factors and stored local transformations; otherwise return `success`, $B,U,V$, the ordered stored local transformations, the reconstruction residual $\\|C_0-U\\begin{bmatrix}B\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}V^*\\|_F$, and the two orthogonality residuals $\\|U^*U-I\\|_F$ and $\\|V^*V-I\\|_F$. The reconstruction uses the saved input $C_0$, not the overwritten work matrix. The exact products of the stored unitary representatives are the theoretical factors; the dense finite-precision accumulators are rounded and their residuals are computed quantities, not certified bounds by themselves. Matrix residuals use the Frobenius norm defined in [[def-frobenius-matrix-norm]].",
