ization nonnegative in both orientations and keeps the left/right vector dimensions correct. Sort the candidate values in nonincreasing order, breaking ties by their original diagonal index, and permute the corresponding columns of the returned triplet vectors in the same way; leave $B_{final}$ and the transformation lists in their algorithmic order. For every candidate triplet $(\\widehat\\sigma_i,\\widehat u_i,\\widehat v_i)$, report $\\|A\\widehat v_i-\\widehat\\sigma_i\\widehat u_i\\|_2$ and $\\|A^*\\widehat u_i-\\widehat\\sigma_i\\widehat v_i\\|_2$. Also report $\\|\\widehat U^*\\widehat U-I\\|_F$ and $\\|\\widehat V^*\\widehat V-I\\|_F$. The reports expose finite-budget and rounding behavior; they do not certify convergence by themselves. Matrix residuals use the Frobenius norm defined in [[def-frobenius-matrix-norm]]. Any additional sparsity cleanup is recorded separately in the deflation record with its discarded-entry perturbation.",
