-          "quote": "Let $C_0\\in\\mathbb F^{M\\times p}$, $M\\ge p$, be the tall orientation used by [[alg-householder-bidiagonalization]]. Suppose the computed bidiagonal reduction and QR sweeps perform $J$ elementary left/right unitary updates. At update $j$, assume the actual active matrix obeys\n$$C_j=L_j^*(C_{j-1}+E_j)R_j+D_j,$$\nwhere $L_j,R_j$ are unitary and $\\eta_j\\ge0$, $\\|E_j\\|_F\\le\\eta_j\\|C_{j-1}\\|_F$, and $D_j$ is the post-transform additive representation of entries discarded by deflation, with $\\delta_j=\\|D_j\\|_F$. Then the returned transformed matrix $C_J$ satisfies\n$$C_0+E=L C_J R^*$$\nfor unitary accumulated factors $L,R$ and some $E$ with\n$$\\|E\\|_F\\le\\left(\\prod_{j=1}^J(1+\\eta_j)-1\\right)\\|C_0\\|_F+\\sum_{j=1}^J\\delta_j\\prod_{\\ell=j+1}^J(1+\\eta_\\ell).$$\nIn the no-deflation case every $\\delta_j=0$. For the successful scaled arithmetic realization [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]], [[lem-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-local-backward-error]] establishes these hypotheses: choose $\\eta_j=\\eta_H(r_j)$ for Householder updates, $\\eta_j=\\eta_G$ for Givens updates with an actual target zero write, and its smaller separate-block coefficient when no matrix entry is overwritten. This covers real/complex left and right updates. Every additional discarded entry is included in $D_j$. Rounded dense accumulators remain separate from these exact represented products.",
+          "quote": "Let $C_0\\in\\mathbb F^{M\\times p}$, $M\\ge p$, be the tall orientation used by [[alg-householder-bidiagonalization]], and let $B_J\\in\\mathbb F^{p\\times p}$ be the final bidiagonal-QR work matrix returned by [[alg-implicit-shifted-bidiagonal-qr-with-deflation]]. Set $C_J=\\begin{bmatrix}B_J\\\\0_{M-p,p}\\end{bmatrix}\\in\\mathbb F^{M\\times p}$. Suppose the computed bidiagonal reduction and QR sweeps perform $J$ stages, each either an elementary left/right unitary update or an identity update for a deflation/cleanup write. At stage $j$, assume the actual active matrix obeys\n$$C_j=L_j^*(C_{j-1}+E_j)R_j+D_j,$$\nwhere $L_j,R_j$ are unitary and $\\eta_j\\ge0$, $\\|E_j\\|_F\\le\\eta_j\\|C_{j-1}\\|_F$, and $D_j$ is the additive representation of entries discarded by deflation or cleanup at that stage, with $\\delta_j=\\|D_j\\|_F$. A deflation/cleanup write is represented by $L_j=R_j=I$, $E_j=0$, and the recorded additive change $D_j$. The deflation record returned by the algorithm identifies each such entry and its old value, so it determines $D_j$. Then the returned tall transformed matrix $C_J$ satisfies\n$$C_0+E=L C_J R^*$$\nfor unitary accumulated factors $L,R$ and some $E$ with\n$$\\|E\\|_F\\le\\left(\\prod_{j=1}^J(1+\\eta_j)-1\\right)\\|C_0\\|_F+\\sum_{j=1}^J\\delta_j\\prod_{\\ell=j+1}^J(1+\\eta_\\ell).$$\nIf no deflation or other cleanup is performed, every $\\delta_j=0$. For the successful scaled arithmetic realization [[alg-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-updates]], [[lem-scaled-complex-householder-and-givens-local-backward-error]] establishes these hypotheses: choose $\\eta_j=\\eta_H(r_j)$ for Householder updates, $\\eta_j=\\eta_G$ for Givens updates with an actual target zero write, and its smaller separate-block coefficient when no matrix entry is overwritten. This covers real/complex left and right updates. Every additional discarded entry is included in $D_j$. Rounded dense accumulators remain separate from these exact represented products.",
